Package: PRIMEeval
Type: Package
Title: Budgeted Sequential Auditing of Paired Model Losses
Version: 0.8.0.9001
Authors@R: person("Hongdong", "Hao", email = "h294866@foxmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"))
Description: Sequential auditing of finite populations of bounded paired model
    loss differences under a shared label-cost budget. Implements public
    width-based sampling, online offset prediction, a two-stage SUPPORT task
    allocator, deterministic support certificates, and separately labelled
    development e-value readouts. Includes deterministic support allocation with affine continuation and
    a charged early proxy reversal guard, explicit historical calibration,
    resumable request-and-update interfaces, and an experimental historical
    query-value allocation option. The implementation is independent of the
    original development directories and does not retrain prediction models.
    Development e-value readouts do not establish global cross-task stopping
    or post-selection error guarantees.
